# validation-pins.env — W-105 (bitty CTX-0931) pinned validation-suite revisions.
#
# Single source of truth for the immutable suite revisions the product change
# path gates against (W-75 pin discipline: exact commits, never branches or
# tags). Shell-sourceable (`set -a; . ./validation-pins.env`) and read by CI
# to form the external checkout refs (`ref:` must be a commit SHA for a
# `repository:` checkout, so an unknown or moving pin fails the workflow
# instead of testing the wrong code).
#
# A pin bump is an owned, reviewed change: refresh the vendored
# compat-fixture snapshots when product tests/scenarios move
# (`scripts/check-compat-fixture-freshness.sh` fails otherwise), re-run the
# thin gates below, and record both revisions (production + suite) with the
# result. After the suite PRs merge, re-pin these to the merge commits.
#
# Tested production revision both suites exercise (bitty origin/main at the
# W-105 move; also recorded in each suite repository Cargo.toml + Cargo.lock).
BITTY_PRODUCTION_REV=9bc73207ab559d4d5de4ef283a4056dc8857de01
# Suite revisions under test (merge commits of bitty-compat-lab#7 and
# bitty-perf#7; bump with the same review + gate discipline).
BITTY_COMPAT_LAB_REPO=bitty-terminal/bitty-compat-lab
BITTY_COMPAT_LAB_REV=6887d08ad7835739cd78c7c04500f879dcc41c17
BITTY_PERF_REPO=bitty-terminal/bitty-perf
BITTY_PERF_REV=73aa233d1318b661dd794f167caccbf2dd7f22bc
